  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Poverty and Descolonization Research Dominican Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project to rethink poverty from a decolonization approach as a perspective to identify the hidden faces of poverty that are overlooked in contemporary literature and to develop a boarder understanding of poverty, particularly the multiple ways in which it is experienced by the communities in which we work. The research will attempt to identify the following elements: What are the historically entrenched relations of power and accumulation that sustain situations of poverty/impoverishment; ho are poverty and wealth and their relationship to colonization defined/understood in key contexts for research.</narrative>
  </description>
